/-!
# Čech acyclicity of rational coverings for discrete Huber pairs

Let `A` be a commutative ring equipped with the discrete topology, `P` a pair of definition of `A`,
and `A⁺` a subring of `A`. On `Spa(A, A⁺)`, every rational open `W = R(T/s)` has coordinate ring
`presentationLimit Aplus W` canonically isomorphic to the algebraic localisation `Aₛ`
(`TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.presentationLimitRationalAlgEquivOfDiscreteTopology`). This file proves
the algebraic denominator criterion and all-degree Čech acyclicity for rational covers over a
discrete pair:

* If a family of rational subsets `(R(Tⱼ/σⱼ))ⱼ` covers `R(T/s)`, the images of the denominators
  `σⱼ` generate the unit ideal of any localisation `S` of `A` away from `s`
  (`TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.span_eq_top_of_discrete_rational_cover`). Consequently, for any
  finite rational cover of `R(T/s)` and any `S`-module `N`, the augmented Čech complex of
  localisations `0 → N → ∏ⱼ N_{σⱼ} → ∏_{j₀ < j₁} N_{σ_{j₀} σ_{j₁}} → ⋯` is exact in every degree.
* The covering hypothesis is essential: over a discrete polynomial ring `k[X]` over an integral
  domain `k` (for instance a field `k` with `A⁺ = k`), the trivial valuation with support `(X)`
  lies in `R({1}/1) \ R({X}/X)`, the ideal generated by `X` in `k[X]₁` is proper, and the
  restriction map `k[X] → k[X, X⁻¹]` is not surjective
  (`exists_mem_rationalSubset_notMem_and_span_ne_top_and_not_surjective_polynomial`).
* For an arbitrary `A`-module `M`, tensoring sections of `presentationLimit` over `A` with `M`
  defines the abelian-group presheaf `presentationLimitTensorAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W M`
  (`V ↦ 𝒪(V) ⊗_A M`) on the opens contained in `W`. For every rational open `W` and every nonempty
  cover `U` of `W` by rational opens (finite or infinite), the augmented Čech complex of
  `presentationLimitTensorAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W M` for `U` is exact in all degrees
  (`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_spaRationalOpens_tensor_of_iSup_eq_of_discreteTopology`).
  Taking `M = A` recovers all-degree Čech acyclicity of `presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf`
  (`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_spaRationalOpens_of_iSup_eq_of_discreteTopology`).

The finite-cover proof identifies the ordered Čech complex of `V ↦ 𝒪(V) ⊗_A M` with the module
Čech complex of localisations of `𝒪(W) ⊗_A M` via `toStrictMonoCechComplex` and relative
localisation (`isLocalization_away_presentationLimit_spaBasicOpen_of_mul`).
Quasi-compactness of rational opens (`isCompact_of_mem_spaRationalFamily`) and the refinement
comparison (`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_of_quasiIso_prod_of_hom`) then extend acyclicity to arbitrary
nonempty rational covers.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.presentationLimitTensorAddCommGrpPresheaf` : the presheaf
  `V ↦ presentationLimit Aplus V ⊗[A] M` of abelian groups on `Set.Iic W`.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.presentationLimitTensorAddCommGrpPresheafUnitIso` : the canonical
  isomorphism `presentationLimitTensorAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W A ≅
  presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.span_eq_top_of_discrete_rational_cover` : if rational subsets
  `R(Tⱼ/σⱼ)` cover `R(T/s)` over a discrete ring `A`, the images of `σⱼ` generate `⊤` in `Aₛ`.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.cechComplexLocalization_exact_of_discrete_rational_cover` : module
  Čech exactness in positive degrees for a finite discrete rational cover.
* `quasiIso_cechAugmentation_spaRationalOpens_tensor_of_iSup_eq_of_discreteTopology` :
  all-degree Čech acyclicity of `𝒪 ⊗_A M` for any nonempty rational cover of a rational open.
* `quasiIso_cechAugmentation_spaRationalOpens_of_iSup_eq_of_discreteTopology` :
  all-degree Čech acyclicity of `𝒪` for any nonempty rational cover of a rational open.

## References

* [T. Wedhorn, *Adic Spaces*][wedhorn_adic] (arXiv:1910.05934v1), Theorem 8.28(c) and
  Corollary 8.35.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite TensorProduct
